"comparison": "Both AVGO and AMD provide customizable silicon platforms for customers targeting high-performance computing and AI workloads, but they differ in underlying technology and flexibility. AVGO provides IP platforms and technology for customers to design custom ASICs, which are built to specific customer specifications (e.g., integrating embedded logic, memory, and SerDes). In contrast, AMD offers FPGAs and Adaptive SoCs, which feature reconfigurable hardware, allowing for post-manufacturing flexibility rather than the fixed, custom nature of ASICs described by AVGO. AVGO focuses on the creation of bespoke silicon for AI/HPC, while AMD focuses on adaptable, reconfigurable platforms for acceleration and embedded systems.",
